On Jul 17, 4:26 pm, "Marcus" <as...@asdfdsf.com> wrote:
> [...] I'd like to be able to play Nethack in text mode if possible.

     The current text mode executable for Windows (that's the
nethack.exe executable which comes along with the nethackW.exe
one when you download binaries for Windows, not the one for MSDOS)
works fine on Vista when run in a window (which is the default
operation--you don't have to do anything in particular to make
it work).  Forcing that window to expand to full screen is the
part that doesn't work (and as is mentioned later in this thread,
is a limitation of Vista rather than something that nethack is
doing or failing to do).

     With suitable choice of font you could probably make the
window used by nethack take up nearly the whole screen, but that
will still be running in a window rather than full screen mode.



